# Issue #1843: +1 raw log_event call in measure_host_load's _log_unavailable
# helper (the rate-limited host_load_unavailable diagnostic event). A
# standalone function in a new module, not an OrchestratorApp method, so it
# has no self.write_gate receiver -- same out-of-wave pattern as
# ci_headroom.py's own _log_unavailable above. Lives at top-level
# charlie_work/host_load.py (not under orchestration/): every top-level def
# in a flat orchestration/ submodule is auto-installed onto OrchestratorApp
# (see workflow_delegation.py), and this module's functions are plain
# standalone helpers with no ``self``, never meant to become members.
